      "extract": "Representation theory provides a powerful set of tools for analyzing systems invariant under the action of some group such as a molecular symmetry group in chemistry or a gauge group in quantum ﬁeld theory. For example, the eigenvalue spectrum of a quantum system is usually com- puted by decomposing the Hilbert space into a direct sum of irreducible representations of the symmetry group and diagonalizing each",
      "extractCut": true
    },
