      ],
      "extract": "Suppose that G is a ﬁnite group. A d-dimensional rep- resentation of G is a group homomorphism from G to the unitary group U(d). A representation is irreducible if the ambient Hilbert space Cd contains no proper subspace invariant under the action of all group elements. It is stan- dard to identify irreps that diﬀer only by a basis change in the ambient Hilbert space. Then any ﬁnite group has a ﬁnite set of irreps.",
      "extractCut": true
    },
