      "extract": "Consider a permutation g ∈Sn. Let c(g) be the number of cycles in g and νj be the length of the j th cycle. Our strategy is to represent the 2n-qubit state |ψg⟩= c(g) \u0003 j =1 Jνj |1n0n⟩ (15) by an MPS. To this end, we need the following lemma. Lemma 2. The current operator Jℓis an MPO with bond dimension ℓ+ 2. Proof. Figure 1 deﬁnes a tensor T ∈C2 ⊗Cℓ+2 ⊗ Cℓ+2 ⊗C2, where C2 represents physical indices and Cℓ+2",
